UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'AI Literacy is still the biggest challenge when it comes to adoption in the corporate and enterprise space.  There are a lot of businesses out there that area going out and "keeping up with the Joneses" by buying Microsoft Copilot or Google Gemini licenses for their employees, and are upset that they aren''t seeing the return on their investment 6 months later.  The reason why is because they are making the investment in the tools, but not making the investment in their employees to teach them. When I say teach them, I mean not only teaching them how to technically use the tools, but how to adjust their way of thinking and how they approach their day to day with an ultra capable new toolset.   AI is not going away any time soon, and more companies and businesses of all sizes are going to continue to feel pressure to start adopting it in their work. If you or your company fit into this category, please, make sure that you are investing in quality training that teaches everyone how to use the tool and focuses on finding practical ways to implement it, ways that are measurable and save actual time in people''s day.  One of the products I lead with at The AI Consulting Lab is corporate training. We sit down with management, or the key employees at a company to do a comprehensive needs analysis to understand what the day to day responsibilities are, and what goes into doing them. Doing this allows us to create meaningful connections in people''s minds when they attend our training, so that it''s something tangible they can understand because it''s something they do almost every day. If you do something that takes you 45 minutes to an hour to do, multiple times per week, and I show you how to do the same task at the same quality in 10 minutes, almost everyone will lock in on it.  The way to succeed with the current level of AI(what we have available today, no smarter) is to find 3-5 use cases that people do within your business, and build custom GPT''s to help reduce the amount of time doing those tasks. If you even get 10% more efficient by doing that, you''re looking at 16 hours saved per employee, per month. If you have a team of 10, call that 160 hours, and 1,600 hours for a team of 100. Valuable time that can be spent doing other high value, or more fulfilling work.  If you''re looking to start implementing more AI in your business in 2025, start with training. We do free 30 minute consults to dig in and find out how to get started, so if you''re interested, check out my profile to schedule time to talk about corporate training.  #chatgpt #ai #aiconsulting #gpt4 #aitraining ' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7462116584321158446';
