UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'Can we reclaim authentic intimacy in an increasingly atomized world? This week on the podcast, I''m joined by Esther Perel, acclaimed psychotherapist, bestselling author, and the visionary voice behind "Where Should We Begin?" We explore her non-judgmental approach to modern relationships, challenging our deranged notions of love in the digital age. We go deep into the vicissitudes of human connection, examining how our quest for security often sabotages the very intimacy we seek. Through her uniquely multicultural lens, Esther highlights how embracing uncertainty—rather than hermetically sealing ourselves from it—might be the key to sustaining desire in long-term relationships. Our conversation charts new territory in understanding modern love—from friendship to long-term partnership to the nature of desire itself. Special Note: If this resonates, check out her newly launched The Desire Bundle—and use code RICH15 for 15% off through December. Now available on YouTube, Spotify, Apple Podcasts and everywhere you enjoy the RRP. Click the link in bio for more. Episode 872. ✌🏼🌱 - Rich' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7438634771980258603';
UPDATE public.stories SET title = 'Tired of ChatGPT''s limited memory? I see questions about this all the time on social, and how to get more memory.  Here''s a solution: create a custom GPT with all your memories instead. To do this, copy ChatGPT''s memories about you into a Word doc, then create a custom GPT, and upload the document. Put in this prompt for your instructions:  You are a helpful assistant to [your name]. Answer questions as per your training. you have a knowledge file full of information about [your name], use it when appropriate, or asked.  You''ll need to update the word doc when you want to add new memories, but otherwise, unlimited memory!  Note: this feature is available on the Paid plan only.  #AI #ChatGPT #CustomGPT #TechTips #aiconsulting ' WHERE slug = 'tiktok-7437638661577051438';
